    "taxonId": 406381,
    "summary": "A small moss whose native origin is not stated, recorded across several continents and Pacific islands. It grows mainly on tree bark and has leaves that twist when dry, each ending in a conspicuous smooth hair-point. Leaf-like reproductive structures occur at stem tips and in upper leaf axils.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s1:p1"],
      "humanEdibility": []
    }
  },
  {
    "taxonId": 411141,
    "summary": "A creeping perennial herb endemic to New Zealand, although also recorded from Sardinia in Europe. It forms loose mats, rooting beyond where its nodding white flowers appear, and can become an aggressive weed in urban areas, wasteland and plant nurseries.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s1:p3", "s1:p5", "s1:p7", "s1:p8"],
      "humanEdibility": []
    }
  },
  {
    "taxonId": 461333,
    "summary": "A feather moss whose native origin is not stated. It has dense branches with crowded, narrow pointed leaves; some leaf tips twist halfway around, and some stems creep underground.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s1:p2", "s1:p5", "s1:p7"],
      "humanEdibility": []
    }
  },
  {
    "taxonId": 465248,
    "summary": "A small red seaweed whose native origin is not stated in this British and Irish account. Its compressed crimson fronds arise from creeping cylindrical runners and have flattened upper branches, blunt tips, hollow interiors and pinched nodes. It grows on rocks and kelp holdfasts in silty pools and below low tide on exposed shores.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s1:p2", "s1:p3"],
      "humanEdibility": []
    }
  },
  {
    "taxonId": 466451,
    "summary": "An upright, spreading annual herb whose native origin is not stated. It bears numerous showy flower spikes above dense, narrow green foliage; the blooms last into autumn and can be used fresh or dried.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s1:p2", "s1:p3"],
      "humanEdibility": []
    }
  },
  {
    "taxonId": 469288,
    "summary": "A red alga whose native origin is not stated, distributed in the English Channel, Atlantic and Mediterranean. Its firm body grades from dark red at the base to bright carmine tips, with upper branches ending in spiny branchlets. It grows on rocky seabeds from shallow water to 70 metres deep.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s1:p2", "s1:p3", "s1:p4"],
      "humanEdibility": []
    }
  },
  {
    "taxonId": 481178,
    "summary": "A bright-green moss whose native origin is not stated, recorded in the Americas, southern and western Europe, Turkey and Macaronesia. It is distinguished by several interrupted leaf rosettes along each stem and slender hair-points that curve back when dry. It also reproduces through small red tubers.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s1:p1"],
      "humanEdibility": []
    }
  },
  {
    "taxonId": 489422,
    "summary": "A genus of about 65 perennial herb species, sometimes low shrubs, distributed across North Africa, Asia and southern Europe; its native origin is not explicitly stated. Members have alternate simple leaves, flower clusters at stem tips, five petals and usually dry capsules.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s2:p1"],
      "humanEdibility": []
    }
  },
  {
    "taxonId": 507596,
    "summary": "A much-branched perennial subshrub native to temperate Asia. It has terminal rounded flower clusters with white, pink or mauve flowers, while its stems and leaves range from nearly hairless to densely hairy. The species is extremely variable across southwestern Asia, and the two subspecies recognized in Pakistan may not be distinct.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s1:p1", "s2:p2"],
      "humanEdibility": []
    }
  },
